---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const schema={"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebApplication","name":"Contractor Bid & Markup Calculator","applicationCategory":"BusinessApplication","operatingSystem":"Web","description":"Build a contractor bid from direct costs, contingency and a target profit margin.","offers":{"@type":"Offer","price":"0","priceCurrency":"USD"},"url":Astro.url.href};
---
<Layout title="Contractor Bid & Markup Calculator | Ozarbox" description="Calculate contractor bid price, markup and profit margin from labor, materials, equipment, subcontractor costs, overhead and contingency.">
<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)}></script>
<section class="tool-wrap container">
<div class="breadcrumbs"><a href={base}Home</a> / <a href={`${base}niche/hidden-business-costs/`}>Hidden business costs</a> / Contractor bid</div>
<div class="tool-head"><div class="eyebrow">Construction estimating</div><h1>Contractor Bid & Markup Calculator</h1><p>Turn direct project costs into a bid that accounts for overhead, contingency and your target profit margin.</p></div>
<div class="tool-box"><div class="form-grid">
<label>Direct labor<input id="labor" type="number" value="18000" min="0" step="0.01" /></label>
<label>Materials<input id="materials" type="number" value="12000" min="0" step="0.01" /></label>
<label>Equipment & subcontractors<input id="other" type="number" value="5000" min="0" step="0.01" /></label>
<label>Project overhead<input id="overhead" type="number" value="3000" min="0" step="0.01" /></label>
<label>Contingency %<input id="contingency" type="number" value="5" min="0" step="0.1" /></label>
<label>Target profit margin %<input id="margin" type="number" value="15" min="0" max="95" step="0.1" /></label>
</div><button id="calculate">Calculate bid</button><div class="result" id="result" aria-live="polite">Enter your values and tap Calculate.</div></div>
<article class="prose"><h2>Markup vs. profit margin</h2><p>Markup and margin are not the same. Markup measures profit against cost, while profit margin measures profit against the final selling price. A bid built around a target margin must divide cost after contingency by <strong>1 − target margin</strong>.</p><h2>Formula</h2><p>Base cost = labor + materials + equipment/subcontractors + project overhead. Contingency-adjusted cost = base cost × (1 + contingency%). Bid = contingency-adjusted cost ÷ (1 − target profit margin%). Markup = (bid − base cost) ÷ base cost.</p><h2>Example</h2><p>Using $18,000 labor, $12,000 materials, $5,000 other direct costs and $3,000 overhead gives a $38,000 base cost. A 5% contingency gives $39,900. At a 15% target margin, the estimated bid is about $46,941.</p><h2>Related tools</h2><p><a href={`${base}niche/labor-burden-by-trade-calculator/`}>Labor Burden Calculator</a> · <a href={`${base}niche/hidden-business-costs/`}>Hidden Business Costs hub</a> · <a href={`${base}niche/accounting/`}>Accounting tools</a></p><h2>Important note</h2><p>This is an estimating aid. Check contract terms, local tax rules, insurance, bonding, labor classifications and project-specific risk before submitting a binding bid.</p></article>
</section>
</Layout>
<script>
const input=(id:string): HTMLInputElement => {
  const el=document.getElementById(id);
  if (!(el instanceof HTMLInputElement)) throw new Error(`Expected input: ${id}`);
  return el;
};
const n=(id:string):number=>Number(input(id).value||0);
const money=(x:number):string=>x.toLocaleString(undefined,{style:'currency',currency:'USD',maximumFractionDigits:2});
const result=document.getElementById('result');
if (!result) throw new Error('Missing result element');
document.getElementById('calculate')?.addEventListener('click',()=>{const base=n('labor')+n('materials')+n('other')+n('overhead'); const cost=base*(1+n('contingency')/100); const bid=n('margin')<100?cost/(1-n('margin')/100):NaN; const profit=bid-cost; const markup=base>0?(bid-base)/base*100:NaN; result.textContent=Number.isFinite(bid)?`Estimated bid: ${money(bid)} | Estimated profit after contingency: ${money(profit)} | Markup on base cost: ${markup.toFixed(2)}%`:'Check your inputs.';});
</script>
